>>
Rule 1 (tensor shape should match between input and output)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= shape(v_1) = shape(v_2)
>>
Rule 3 (tensor input must be valid for randint_like)
{v_1 : tensor} |= v_1 ≠ null
>>
Rule 4 (low and high parameters should be integers)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : int} |= v_1 ≠ null ∧ v_2 ≠ null
>>
Rule 5 (low parameter must be less than high parameter)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : int} |= v_1 < v_2
>>
Rule 6 (input tensor must have at least one dimension)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) > 0
>>
Rule 14 (high parameter should be greater than low parameter)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : int} |= v_2 > v_1
